  "notes": [
    "Optional voice packages. The app offers them in the setup assistant and under Voices: packages for the app language are preselected, the user deselects what they do not want. Downloads start only after the user confirms. Windows voices need no package.",
    "Taken over from GT Toolz with the same pins and checksums: only voices whose license clearly allows use (free, closed source, donations without perks). Decisions 2026-10-18, see docs/03-security.md.",
    "Rejected Piper voices: en_US-lessac (research only) and everything finetuned from it (ryan, kerstin, thorsten, amy).",
    "Both engines contain espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later). Users download them from the original source; Stream Toolz only runs them as separate programs.",
    "Engines come per platform (\"platform\": \"<os>-<arch>\" as Node reports it, e.g. \"win32-x64\", \"linux-x64\"); voice models are the same everywhere. A package without a file for the running platform is not offered.",
    "Added 2026-10-22 to try out (the user: only voices free for open-source use): standard licenses only (MIT, BSD, Apache, CC0 or public domain, CC BY with attribution); custom terms such as \"for any legal and ethical purpose\" count as no. English Piper voices trained from scratch on public-domain recordings, and CSS10 German (BSD-3-Clause, runs in sherpa-onnx without espeak).",
    "sherpa-onnx packages (Kokoro, CSS10 German) left the catalogue on 2026-10-28: the engine reads its text argument in the Windows ANSI code page (docs/05-release-check.md)."
  ],
